{
  "id": "COMPOUND:29801 - PROTEIN:1642",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that (2R)-pentan-2-ol may interact with Proto-oncogene tyrosine-protein kinase Src through multiple indirect pathways. The drug is identified as a target of several compounds, including 8-O-(P-Coumaroyl)-1(10)E,4(5)E-Humuladien-8-Ol and 1-O-beta-D-Glucopyranosyl anthranilate, all of which are linked to Src via their respective targets. Similarly, (2R)-pentan-2-ol is also associated with Non-receptor tyrosine-protein kinase TNK1, which in turn targets Src. These findings suggest that (2R)-pentan-2-ol may exert its biological effects through a network of downstream kinases, potentially modulating Src activity in a complex regulatory cascade. The integration of these pathways highlights the drug's potential to influence Src-mediated signaling, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
